[{"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186124644, "id": "facdd9e7-8fcb-5ad1-b9c1-82c0f753df1a", "title": "Evaluating a Partial Derivative at a Point"}, "question": {":question/problem": "For the function $f(x,y)=2 x^{2} y^{2}+4 x y,$ evaluate $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ at the point $(-1,1).$", ":question/worked-solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants:\n\nAdditionally, we use the sum and constant multiple rules for differentiation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} y^{2}+4 x y) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2 x^{2} y^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x y) \\\\  & =2 y^{2}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x^{2})+4 y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =2 y^{2}\\cdot (2 x)+4 y\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =4 x y^{2}+4 y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the partial derivative at the point $(-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}{|}_{(-1,1)} & =4 (-1) (1)^{2}+4 (1) \\\\  & =-4+(4) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy", ":question/id": "9a49be4e-a65d-5fd8-9249-d7a3cae0914f", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "2ceb1634-5290-59c5-8cf2-c200fc4bb9aa", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "ac0d978f-cfaf-5a13-8661-544cb29f4578", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "-8"}, {":answer/id": "ae943ffe-36e9-512c-beda-f872e731aa91", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "-4"}, {":answer/id": "fbb44bf8-e9ac-53b9-a049-de8843315ca9", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "8"}, {":answer/id": "688f0d0b-70cb-56c3-9110-1f8a756db36f", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "4"}, {":answer/id": "aaafc44b-0a10-54e7-aa36-22a370550071", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "0"}], ":answer-field/correct": [":answer/id", "aaafc44b-0a10-54e7-aa36-22a370550071"]}]}, "generation": {"version": "partial-point-dra